{{also|re-lay}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|Relay (disambiguation)}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|relai||reserve pack of hounds|lang=frm}}, from {{term|relaier||to exchange tired animals for fresh|lang=frm}}; literally, "to leave behind", from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|relaier||to leave behind|lang=fro}}, from {{term|re-|lang=fro}} + {{term|laier||to leave|lang=fro}}, of uncertain origin.

====Pronunciation====
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɹiːleɪ/}}
*{{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɹileɪ/}}
*{{rhymes|iːleɪ}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|hunting|now|_|rare}} A new set of [[hound]]s. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
# {{context|now|_|chiefly|historical}} A new set of [[horse]]s kept along a specific [[route]] so that they can replace animals that are tired. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
# A [[series]] of [[vehicle]]s travelling in [[sequence]]. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
# {{context|athletics}} A [[track and field]] discipline where runners take turns in carrying a [[baton]] from start to finish. Most common events are 4x100 meter and 4x400 meter competitions. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# {{electronics}} An electrical [[actuator]] that allows a relatively small electrical [[voltage]] or [[current]] to control a larger voltage or current. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}

